WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.412
Some control families no cloud
provider can close for you.

2
00:00:03.412 --> 00:00:05.363
The first is program management.

3
00:00:05.363 --> 00:00:09.387
NIST marks the whole family as
deployed organization-wide,

4
00:00:09.387 --> 00:00:13.659
outside the system baselines
and independent of impact level,

5
00:00:13.659 --> 00:00:18.424
and FedRAMP lists no class for any
of its 37 controls and enhancements.

6
00:00:18.424 --> 00:00:22.721
The obligation comes from
FISMA and OMB's Circular A-130,

7
00:00:22.721 --> 00:00:27.950
and it binds the agency whether or
not it uses a single cloud service.

8
00:00:27.950 --> 00:00:31.412
No resolver, overlay or
enforcement point can write an

9
00:00:31.412 --> 00:00:35.413
organization's risk tolerance
or appoint its senior official.

10
00:00:35.413 --> 00:00:40.116
These controls close when the artifact
exists, a named official has approved it,

11
00:00:40.116 --> 00:00:44.249
and the agency can show it is still
followed: the security program plan,

12
00:00:44.249 --> 00:00:47.811
the appointed senior agency
information security officer,

13
00:00:47.811 --> 00:00:52.371
a risk strategy with a signed tolerance
statement, a process that keeps every

14
00:00:52.371 --> 00:00:57.288
system's plan of action comparable, and
one organization-wide monitoring strategy.

15
00:00:57.288 --> 00:00:59.576
One distinction matters to an assessor.

16
00:00:59.576 --> 00:01:01.984
The program inventory lists systems;

17
00:01:01.984 --> 00:01:05.637
each system's component
inventory lists what's inside it.

18
00:01:05.637 --> 00:01:06.980
The two must agree.
